Cet, Talon Lieutenant wrote:
>
> If chaotic and capable of killing shopkeepers, is it beneficial to
> activate the Keystone Kops for whatever goods they might have?

Generally kops are created with equipment that sucks.  They come with
pies and rubber hoses.  Pies are poor food.  Rubber hoses are completely
useless against thick skinned monsters.  But if you plan on doing a
polypile session the quantity of objects matters and triggering the kops
will generate a lot of polypile fodder.  Most food items from polymorph
are better than pies. Almost all weapons from polymorph are better than
rubber hose.  If you're doing a polypile for weapons you're not in a
good situation - Artifacts and athames are never created by polymorph.

There are a lot of kops generated.  If you're strong enough to
just barely survive the combat there might be enough to get another
level of XP out of them.  If you're strong enough to not worry about
surviving the combat then it's not worth it just for the points.

If you want death drops it could be worth stealing from shop after shop
until the kop types are extinct.  There are easier methods to generate
tons of monsters.


